[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4534112744","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119687#issuecomment-4534112744","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119687","id":4534112744,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDkER6A","user":{"login":"vilmt","id":158532337,"node_id":"U_kgDOCXMC8Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158532337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt","html_url":"https://github.com/vilmt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-25T12:05:02Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T12:05:02Z","body":"I can confirm this issue is still present in 4.7 beta 3.\n\nI researched this a little more, and this behavior is standard for `PhysicsDirectSpaceState3D.cast_motion`. The following is stated in the documentation:\n\n> Note: Any Shape3Ds that the shape is already colliding with e.g. inside of, will be ignored. Use collide_shape() to determine the Shape3Ds that the shape is already colliding with.\n\nThis behavior seems reasonable for the physics method, but feels unintuitive as the default behavior of ShapeCast3D. Maybe we could implement a bool field like `ignore_immediate_collisions`? When enabled, the shape cast would ignore initial overlaps (the current behavior). When disabled, the shape cast would first check for immediate overlaps and report them with unsafe fraction 0.0.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4534112744/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4534118674","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119687#issuecomment-4534118674","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119687","id":4534118674,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDkEpEg","user":{"login":"vilmt","id":158532337,"node_id":"U_kgDOCXMC8Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158532337?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt","html_url":"https://github.com/vilmt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vilmt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-25T12:05:57Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T12:05:57Z","body":"My bad, closed accidentally.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4534118674/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4535577151","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119687#issuecomment-4535577151","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119687","id":4535577151,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDldqPw","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-25T16:01:45Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T16:01:45Z","body":"This is probably something do debug, it might be something that is complicated to change and not necessarily expected that the shape will reporting a collision if it collides *before* starting the sweep, and some might depend on the specific behavior when inside shapes, in the example in the report the behavior is clearly \"odd\" but there can be situations where it makes sense to ignore the current collision to detect the exit point for example","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4535577151/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5704449356","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119687#issuecomment-5704449356","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119687","id":5704449356,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVAL9TA","user":{"login":"bmorledge-hampton19","id":22180776,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTgwNzc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22180776?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bmorledge-hampton19","html_url":"https://github.com/bmorledge-hampton19","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bmorledge-hampton19/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bmorledge-hampton19/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bmorledge-hampton19/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bmorledge-hampton19/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bmorledge-hampton19/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bmorledge-hampton19/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bmorledge-hampton19/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bmorledge-hampton19/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bmorledge-hampton19/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T21:01:25Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T21:01:25Z","body":"This behavior was also unexpected to me and has caused me a lot of headache... A toggle to report immediate collisions in ShapeCast2D/3D would be much appreciated.\n\nAdditionally, while the documentation for the ShapeCast classes states:\n> Immediate collision overlaps can be done with the [target_position](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_shapecast3d.html#class-shapecast3d-property-target-position) set to Vector3(0, 0, 0) and by calling [force_shapecast_update()](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_shapecast3d.html#class-shapecast3d-method-force-shapecast-update) within the same physics frame.\n\nIt's still not clear that this doesn't happen with a non-zero target position. At the very least, the documentation should be updated to explicitly state that immediate collisions are not reported by default.\n\nWas a proposal ever opened for this? I can't seem to find one, and I'd be happy to write one up.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5704449356/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]